---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../../components/PageHero.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="The counter and the chats can share a stock list." description="For product retailers selling in person and taking remote orders.">
<PageHero eyebrow="The Kora product plan" title="The counter and the chats can share a stock list." lede="For product retailers selling in person and taking remote orders." />
<section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14 prose-kora">
<h2>Keep variants distinct</h2>
<p>Record size, colour and pack separately. Confirm opening stock, then keep counter sales and remote reservations in the same ledger.</p>
<h2>Give staff a quick way to record sales</h2>
<p>A walk-in purchase needs a simple sale-and-handover flow. If staff do not record it, software cannot know the shelf has changed.</p>
<h2>Start with one location</h2>
<p>The founding pilot is being scoped around one stock location per business. Storefront and WhatsApp automation will build on the same core.</p>
<p><a href="/pilot" class="btn btn-primary">Explore the founding pilot</a></p>
</section>
</BaseLayout>
